        "id": 5017,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-03T14:25:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;beevolant&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"beevolant\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>At the end of the game only The Wraith was alive (and only because every turn at least one incapacitated player had her play her innate power of reduce the next two damage (which stacks!), and she had fewer than 5 hit points. Awesome.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually that brings up a question I was somewhat curious. The rules do state that you can not use the same power in a single turn, but if it is a fallen hero that uses their incap power to allow a player to use an additional power would that allow them to use the same power they used during the same turn? Maybe one of the creators can give use the satisfaction of knowing, because I personally have mixed feelings about it.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:33.868Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
