      {
        "id": 20617,
        "name": "WriterRyan",
        "username": "WriterRyan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/writerryan/{size}/2710_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-03T15:42:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>While the official ruling comes down to Christopher, I took the liberty of looking a few things up in the rule book.</p>\n<p>From the turn order section:<br>\n<span class=\"bbcode-i\">Power - This Hero’s player may choose to use one Power from one of their cards in play which has a Power.  Note: even if a Hero may use multiple Powers in a turn, each instance of a Power may only be used once per turn.</span></p>\n<p>From the glossary:<br>\n[i]Power: An ability possessed by Heroes that can be used during a Heroâ€™s Power phase.  A given Power may only be used once by a Hero during that Heroâ€™s Power phase, even if that Hero is allowed to use more than one Power during their Power phase.</p>\n<p>turn: The portion of the game during which all of the actions associated with a given deck take place.  The three types of turns in Sentinels of the Multiverse are Hero turns, Villain turns, and Environment turns.  [/i]</p>\n<p>This isn’t truly official, but it sounds to me like a power may be used multiple times during a round and that the usage is only limited to once per turn.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:45.574Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5017,
        "topic_slug": "power-usage-within-a-round",
