        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "While the official ruling comes down to Christopher, I took the liberty of looking a few things up in the rule book.\n\nFrom the turn order section:\n[i]Power - This Hero's player may choose to use one Power from one of their cards in play which has a Power.  Note: even if a Hero may use multiple Powers in a turn, each instance of a Power may only be used once per turn.[/i]\n\nFrom the glossary:\n[i]Power: An ability possessed by Heroes that can be used during a Heroâ€™s Power phase.  A given Power may only be used once by a Hero during that Heroâ€™s Power phase, even if that Hero is allowed to use more than one Power during their Power phase.\n\nturn: The portion of the game during which all of the actions associated with a given deck take place.  The three types of turns in Sentinels of the Multiverse are Hero turns, Villain turns, and Environment turns.  [/i]\n\nThis isn't truly official, but it sounds to me like a power may be used multiple times during a round and that the usage is only limited to once per turn.",
