      {
        "id": 20618,
        "name": "Christopher",
        "username": "Christopher",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-03T17:44:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ryan’s got it, but let me break it down a bit further.  When an incapacitated Hero allows another Hero to use a power, that Hero doesn’t get to use an additional power on their own turn; rather, they use the power immediately, on the incapacitated Hero’s turn.  Thus, they could use the same power multiple times in the same <span class=\"bbcode-b\">round</span>, but not in the same <span class=\"bbcode-b\">turn</span>.</p>\n<p>Thanks for your question!  I hope this helps.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:45.668Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
